Technique bookkeeping:
Discipline naming: reuse an appropriate existing discipline by ID before creating another. A new discipline names a reusable tradition or field, such as Spellcasting, Martial Arts or Psionics when supported by the setting and established training; prefer the actual skill name when it already names that practice. Its description explains the category, not just the current move. Do not copy generic example labels, invent a separate discipline for each spell/effect, or return unresolved placeholders such as DISCIPLINE_NAME or DISCIPLINE_DESCRIPTION. Access requirements come from established qualifications; there is no default minimum skill rank of 2.
{% if committedTechniqueResults and committedTechniqueResults.length %}
The committedTechniqueResults records have ALREADY applied their exact costs, effects and acquisitions. Do not extract another heal, damage, need debit, status gain, or learned technique for those mutations. Report an optional receipt notification instead:
<techniqueNotification><operationId>exact operation ID</operationId><mutationId>exact effect mutationId</mutationId></techniqueNotification>
An existing healRecover, environmentalStatusDamage, attackDamage, or statusEffectChange event referring to that exact technique effect may instead contain <techniqueReceipt><operationId>exact operation ID</operationId><mutationId>exact effect mutationId</mutationId></techniqueReceipt>. Only that linked effect is suppressed. Do not link independent damage/healing/status changes, even on the same target. Failed checks have no successful effect to reapply. Technique cost notification IDs are operationId followed by ':cost:' and the exact cost key. Acquisition notification IDs are operationId followed by ':change:' and its zero-based techniqueChanges index. Never suppress a needed death/incapacitation decision.
{% endif %}
A completed lesson, teaching item, independent discovery, or actual training/story milestone can teach a technique without forcing a cast. Use <techniqueChange><command>XML-escaped JSON command</command></techniqueChange>. Command fields: kind (learn, improve, evidence), actorId, techniqueId, provenance {kind, sourceId when relevant, reason}. Learn may include definitionRevision and a candidate/candidateDiscipline when no catalogue definition exists. For a new ordinary healing candidate use revision.recipe {"recipeId":"standard-healing","skillName":"actual relevant skill","attributeName":"actual relevant attribute","resourceProfileId":"exact applicable profile ID","effectId":"restore"}; include prerequisites, self/single target and check, and omit numeric costs, failureCosts, effects and balance. Use only the actor's balanceAuthoring choices; do not invent a profile or unsupported area/mixed healing. Reuse equivalent common definitions. For managed healing, Improve includes improvement {"stepId":"exact allowed saved-policy step ID"} and actual unused evidenceIds with justified provenance/reason, and omits mechanics. Choose the owner's saved-policy steps from that learned technique's balanceImprovements; do not change numbers, resource vectors, targets or effects yourself. A complete next mechanics revision remains available only for nonhealing custom techniques. Evidence includes {kind,description}; the engine supplies its identity and current time. Use authoritative IDs and facts, never guessed mechanics or invented qualifications. Do not ask the actor to repeat known stats. Use this only for completed meaningful learning/training, never automatic per-cast upgrades or an extra progression currency. Existing source and acquisition prerequisites still apply. No techniqueChange is needed for a mutation already in committedTechniqueResults.
